1
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,553
We still have a big problem.

2
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:55,138
<i>It's La Morte Bianca.</i>

3
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:00,977
Mikoy, watch over your brother.

4
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,270
But, please,

5
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:05,190
update me if something happens.

6
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:07,650
Don't worry, sweetheart,
I'll be back soon.

7
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:16,076
What did she say?

8
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:19,621
She said she was coming for us,
to torture us.

9
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:21,498
‪Oh!

10
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:32,592
I told you.

11
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,131
Don't worry about me, Viktor.

12
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,592
I'm not afraid of that witch!

13
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:14,444
do whatever you want.

14
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,572
This is all your fault, Alex.

15
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:06,955
You're such an idiot.

16
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:13,962
Every life that was put at risk…
That's all because of you.

17
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:30,728
But it's true, sir.

18
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:37,568
the enemy outsmarted us.

19
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:40,071
If only I had listened when they said

20
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:43,825
Mikoy and Chiara were among the enemy,
none of this would've happened.

21
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:47,036
I was too focused on my instincts.

22
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:50,081
That's why we're in this situation now.

23
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:53,626
If you had listened to us,

24
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:59,090
we never would've learned all of this.

25
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:08,349
We never would've learned
about the bomb's existence

26
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:11,311
if it weren't for Chiara.

27
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:13,271
You gave her a chance,

28
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:16,274
and you're the only one
who thought of doing that.

29
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:20,653
Alex.

30
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:27,744
Because a lot of people believe in you.

31
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:31,706
Trust isn't just something
other people give you.

32
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:34,792
You have to give it to yourself too.

33
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:48,097
We're not perfect.

34
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:50,808
What's important is,

35
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:54,812
we're not doing our job halfway, okay?

36
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:59,358
I see all the sacrifices you make,
everything you do,

37
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:02,070
to keep our country a safer place,

38
00:06:03,571 --> 00:06:05,114
and that's what matters.

39
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:09,660
If we're going to fight,

40
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:11,871
we give it our all.

41
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,542
So I can beat you first.

42
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:03,422
Then untie me. Let's settle this.

43
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,603
You sure do talk a lot.

44
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:22,316
You're like a parrot,
calling my husband weak over and over.

45
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:27,822
But the truth is, you're the weak one.

46
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:29,907
Why are you so obsessed with my daughter?

47
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:33,703
Because she's done what you never could.

48
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:33,596
Alice…

49
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:36,158
- Bok? Bok!
- Hey!

50
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:38,536
What are you doing here?

51
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:40,162
Why are you out of bed?

52
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:41,414
There you are.

53
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:43,124
- Seriously?
- I thought…

54
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:44,208
Come here.

55
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:47,295
- I thought you were upset because…
- Careful.

56
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:50,298
I took a bullet for someone else.

57
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:54,093
What? Wait, are you still high
on anesthesia?

58
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,721
Why would I leave you over that?

59
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,441
We're face-to-face now.

60
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:11,444
My fist can easily
land right on your face, you know.

61
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:16,574
So,

62
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,368
what happens to us now?

63
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:23,998
We managed to extract Angelito, but

64
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:27,501
we failed to recover the bomb.

65
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:37,386
La Morte Bianca has already made her move,

66
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:42,892
We'll attack before dawn.

67
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:57,948
Sweetheart, you should get
some sleep while you can.

68
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:08,084
I can't stop thinking about Mom and Dad.

69
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:14,548
It feels like it's been forever
since I last heard from them.

70
00:11:15,549 --> 00:11:17,051
I'm worried.

71
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:21,305
I don't know what else
La Morte Bianca is capable of

72
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,474
now that she has the bomb.

73
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:29,355
Well,

74
00:11:29,897 --> 00:11:33,067
knowing your parents, sweetheart,

75
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:36,070
they would never give up without a fight.

76
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:37,613
So I'm sure

77
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:41,242
they'll survive whatever danger
comes their way.

78
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:46,872
Come on.

79
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,186
<i>I'm already outside the facility.</i>

80
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:24,743
Agent Alex, this is for Chiara Valtrovi.

81
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:28,080
For me?

82
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:27,616
You're not weak.

83
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:32,580
You just have a good heart,
and in this cruel world, if…

84
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:36,083
you have a heart, they call you weak.

85
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,086
Listen to me

86
00:14:39,795 --> 00:14:41,547
and to your heart.

87
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:27,927
You're right. I still do.

88
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:33,182
Yes, this is how we should be.

89
00:15:34,266 --> 00:15:37,561
We'll get through this.
Just hang in there, okay?

90
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,148
Hang in there.

91
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:43,943
Hang in there.

92
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:56,622
Come on, let's go!

93
00:16:04,546 --> 00:16:07,049
La Morte Bianca is just messing with us.

94
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:15,766
She'll pay for this.

95
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:19,144
I'll make sure she pays for this!

96
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:39,206
<i>But the truth is, you're the weak one.</i>

97
00:16:39,289 --> 00:16:41,166
<i>You're obsessed with my daughter. Why?</i>

98
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:45,921
<i>Because she accomplished</i>
<i>what you never could.</i>

99
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:19,038
I told our agents

100
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:21,165
to lock down this hospital
and look for the person--

101
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:26,378
I'm going to make La Morte Bianca pay.

102
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:28,672
Sweetheart, I can't let you do that.

103
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:30,716
Can we hear the plan first?

104
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:32,801
Mikoy, we're out of time.

105
00:17:33,343 --> 00:17:35,304
Should I wait until La Morte Bianca

106
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:37,681
sends me my parents' heads?

107
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:46,065
For now, let's regroup at HQ.

108
00:17:48,942 --> 00:17:50,486
What about my brother?

109
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:57,159
By now, Mario and Tess
should already be with him.

110
00:17:57,242 --> 00:17:58,869
Looking after him.

111
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:00,913
Mikoy.

112
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:05,918
Don't worry.

113
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:13,342
Mikoy? Mikoy.

114
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,594
- Mom? Mom!
- My son!

115
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:16,637
- Mikoy.
- Mom.

116
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,722
- Son, are you okay?
- I'm okay.

117
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:20,682
- Angelito!
- Son.

118
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:21,767
Angelito.

119
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,435
How's your brother?

120
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:24,937
Mom, Angelito is okay.

121
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,106
The doctor said he's stable.

122
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:28,941
He just needs plenty of rest.

123
00:18:29,024 --> 00:18:30,234
If you need to leave,

124
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:31,902
- The doctor said he'll be fine.
- go ahead.

125
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:32,861
Oh, and how about you?

126
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:34,321
We'll take care of things here.

127
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,365
- Are you okay?
- I'll hold down the fort.

128
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:42,412
Chiara.

129
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:44,832
Thank you, Dad.

130
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:46,750
Dad.

131
00:19:00,389 --> 00:19:02,141
You're going to cry again.

132
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:09,189
Because I'm so frustrated.

133
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:14,695
Ever since I got to that safe house,

134
00:19:14,778 --> 00:19:17,489
all I've done is cry.

135
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:23,328
When Angelito wasn't with us, I cried.

136
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:28,292
And now that he's safe, I'm still crying.

137
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,131
That's only natural.

138
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:37,759
We've been through so much.

139
00:19:40,679 --> 00:19:44,099
My emotions are all over the place, Mario.

140
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:47,352
This is exactly how I felt when

141
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:49,980
Mikoy got shot.

142
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:52,733
It was so hard, so overwhelming.

143
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:55,819
I couldn't do anything.

144
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:58,906
See? I'm crying again.

145
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:01,575
That's not true.

146
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:04,870
It is.

147
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:10,542
Mikoy accepted that mission

148
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:13,754
to protect us.

149
00:20:14,838 --> 00:20:16,840
And Angelito

150
00:20:18,508 --> 00:20:20,469
studied hard.

151
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,889
He devoted himself to community outreach

152
00:20:23,972 --> 00:20:26,558
just to give us a better life.

153
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:28,894
But me, as their mother,

154
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:31,980
I can't help them.

155
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:35,651
Shouldn't I be the one protecting them

156
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:38,487
when they're sick or in danger?

157
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:41,573
I'm not doing anything. All I do is cry.

158
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:47,079
My love, there's a saying.

159
00:20:57,631 --> 00:20:59,049
What that means is,

160
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:02,511
you need to rest too.

161
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:10,394
How can anyone depend on you
if you're drained?

162
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:14,982
How can our children lean on you

163
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:17,609
if you have nothing left to give?

164
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:25,701
You just don't realize it,

165
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:30,455
but even little things

166
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:33,834
can mean so much.

167
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:39,006
Plus,

168
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:42,968
you're an amazing cook.

169
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:45,804
No, really.

170
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:48,598
I'm serious. That's a--

171
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:51,059
Tess, that's a big deal.

172
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:54,021
- How so?
- Seriously!

173
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:56,231
No, think about… Think about it.

174
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:00,485
No one wants to go into battle hungry.

175
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:04,197
They might die of hunger first,

176
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:06,408
before a bullet ever gets them.

177
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:41,711
Your turn. You share something with me.

178
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:45,173
I just don't understand.

179
00:23:45,715 --> 00:23:48,468
How did La Morte Bianca know
where we were?

180
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:51,096
How did she know where to send the box?

181
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:53,431
I thought our location was top-secret

182
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:55,267
and only the agents knew about it.

183
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:03,108
How else do you explain what happened?

184
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:07,779
Someone is feeding information
to the enemy.

185
00:24:16,413 --> 00:24:17,998
Just kill us!

186
00:24:18,915 --> 00:24:20,959
Aren't you allergic with traitors?!

187
00:24:21,042 --> 00:24:22,878
Where is your courage?

188
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:45,483
There's no place where she won't hear us.

189
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:47,527
We need someone
from the inside to help us.
